pwqgen for Android is based on passwdqc by Openwall:
https://www.openwall.com/passwdqc/  https://github.com/openwall/passwdqc

Credits:
- Solar Designer (Openwall): author of passwdqc, including the
  passwdqc_random() passphrase generator this app ports, and curator of
  its word list.
- Dmitry V. Levin: author of the pwqgen command-line program (2008-2009),
  later updated by Solar Designer (2016, 2021).
- Dianelos Georgoudis: author of the MakePass word list (1997, public
  domain) that passwdqc's word list comes from.

Files derived from passwdqc:
- src/generator.rs is a Rust port of passwdqc_random.c
  (Copyright (c) 2000-2002,2005,2008,2010,2013,2016,2021 by Solar Designer).
- src/words/en.txt holds the first 4096 words of wordset_4k.c, which is in
  the public domain (word list from MakePass by Dianelos Georgoudis).
- tests/gen_vectors.c builds passwdqc's own C code to produce the test
  vectors in tests/vectors.txt.

Other word lists (not derived from passwdqc):
- src/words/fr.txt, es.txt, de.txt, ru.txt and la.txt were generated by
  tools/wordlists (see its README.md) and are part of this app under its
  0BSD license.  They were selected using word counts from Mozilla Common
  Voice sentence collections (CC0 1.0), Project Gutenberg books (public
  domain), public-domain Russian prose from Russian Wikisource (texts
  marked PD-old-70), and, for Latin, the WORDS dictionary data by
  William A. Whitaker (1936-2010):
  "Permission is hereby freely given for any and all use of program and
  data."

